1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,850
Her son forwards the ticket. Muse Spark reads it; the journey is built: HYD → DOH → DFW, 15 stages.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:21,850
Her voice note: “start my trip.” She hears: “All right. Your trip has started. I will tell you what to do when it is time.”

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:33,850
Check-in, at its time — her phone (right): the card and the note. “Go to the Qatar Airways counter. Give passport and ticket. Hand over the big bag. Take the boarding pass.”

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,850
Every stage fires on the journey's clock: security, gate, boarding, the flight, Doha. Code owns the timing.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,850
Doha. Her next gate is not announced yet — and that is exactly what she is told.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:01,850
A verified operations event sets gate D14 (simulated, labelled). Her phone: the new card and note. His phone: the update.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:17,850
Her voice note: “Where is my gate?” She hears: “Your Qatar Airways flight leaves from gate D14. Again: gate D14. See the card.”

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:32,850
Her photo of a sign. SAM 3.1 finds the board, Spark reads it: gates B. She hears: “This board is not your gate. Yours is D14. Look for boards that say D.”

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:44,850
Her voice note: “I'm lost.” She gets her card and calm words; her son gets a message. No one claims to know where she is.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:58,050
Boarding, the long flight, Dallas: arrivals, immigration (she answers the officer herself), baggage, exit.

11
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:06,050
Outside, she presses “I'm here.” Her son's phone: journey complete.

